  "documentation": {
    "documents": [
      {
        "id": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "title": "Analyzer_X200_Service_Manual.pdf",
        "instrumentId": "a2d7b449-814f-47a7-9b0c-306430830ca8",
        "documentType": "service_manual",
        "filePath": "C:\\Users\\PCama\\Documents\\Portfolio\\ivA-Troubleshooter\\documents\\instruments\\Analyzer_X200\\Analyzer_X200_Service_Manual.pdf",
        "uploadedAt": "2026-09-23T00:47:16.274Z"
      }
    ],
    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "9096842b-c5e7-40b4-b438-faa8d56657d8",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "pageNumber": 1,
        "width": 612,
        "height": 792,
        "rawText": "The BioMed Analyzer X200 is a fully automated, random-access clinical chemistry analyzer capable of executing up to 800 photometric tests per hour. Analytical precision relies on synchronous closed-loop coordination between the Fluidics Aspiration/Dispense manifold, the 12-wavelength diffraction grating photometer, and dual robotic pipetting arms with capacitive liquid level detection.\n\nThis technical manual provides authorized Field Service Engineers (FSE) with factory diagnostic thresholds, calibration procedures, alarm code resolution trees, and safety compliance directives.\n\nBIOHAZARD & HIGH VOLTAGE MANDATORY WARNING: All patient sera and fluidic waste lines must be treated as potentially infectious. Wear PPE (gloves, eye protection). Mains AC line voltages (100-240V) exist within the rear power distribution bay. Adhere strictly to LOTO protocols.",
        "thumbnailUrl": null,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.745Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "637e60c6-957e-4496-a6ae-ec3aea9224d5",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "pageNumber": 2,
        "width": 612,
        "height": 792,
        "rawText": "Hydraulic Operating Parameter Limits:\n\n| Operating Parameter | Nominal Target | Min Allowable | Max Allowable | Unit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Manifold Baseline Pressure | 120.0 | 114.0 | 126.0 | kPa |\n| Degasser Vacuum Level | -80.0 | -85.0 | -75.0 | kPa |\n| Dispense Syringe Stroke | 250.0 | 249.5 | 250.5 | uL |\n| De-bubble Purge Velocity | 50.0 | 45.0 | 55.0 | uL/s |\n| Sensor Zero Offset Limit | 0.0 | -1.2 | +1.2 | kPa |\n\n• Syringe Dispense Pump P-102 (P/N 948-230-01): 250 uL ceramic piston displacement mechanism.\n• Manifold Pressure Transducer PS-23 (P/N 948-510-23): Piezo-resistive stainless sensor on central block.\n• Solenoid Pinch Valve V-04 (P/N 948-310-04): 3-way high-velocity PTFE isolate valve.\n• Replacement Plunger Seal Upgrade Kit (P/N SP-948-230-01): Mandated by Service Bulletin SB-2026-014.",
        "thumbnailUrl": null,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.753Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "2fbd6db0-1c1e-41ca-91c4-7ebcd4f9d8a9",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "pageNumber": 3,
        "width": 612,
        "height": 792,
        "rawText": "STEP 1: Line Depressurization & Safety Verification\nOpen Service Utilities > Fluidics Diagnostics > Depressurize Manifold. Verify digital readout drops to 0.0 kPa.\n\nSTEP 2: Physical Pressure Transducer Calibration Check\nConnect NIST-traceable Digital Manometer 948-CAL-01 to Quick-Disconnect test port TP-FL-01 on the central manifold.\nExecute 3-minute continuous DI water prime sequence at 50 uL/s.\n\nDECISION BRANCH A: Physical Manometer vs Telemetry Divergence\n• If physical manometer reads within 114.0 - 126.0 kPa, but software telemetry reports < 114.0 kPa:\n  Cause: Transducer drift or zero-offset error in Pressure Sensor PS-23 (P/N 948-510-23).\n  Corrective Action: Recalibrate zero offset via PROC-PUMP-CALIBRATION. If offset exceeds +/- 1.2 kPa, replace sensor with assembly SP-948-510-23.\n\nDECISION BRANCH B: True Physical Pressure Decay\n• If physical manometer ALSO reads < 114.0 kPa or exhibits decay > 1.5 kPa over 60 seconds:\n  Cause: Mechanical seal bypass in Syringe Pump P-102 or internal micro-tearing in Solenoid Valve V-04.\n  Corrective Action: Replace P-102 ceramic plunger wash seals using Upgraded Kit SP-948-230-01. Refer to Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 for proper torque specifications (1.2 Nm).",
        "thumbnailUrl": null,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.757Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "5c9bfaea-bcc4-495d-bea3-3290086587f5",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "pageNumber": 4,
        "width": 612,
        "height": 792,
        "rawText": "FMEA Matrix & Service Bulletin Compliance:\n\n| Failure Mode Code | Severity | Occur | Detect | RPN | Mandatory Action Protocol |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FM-FLUIDICS-PRESSURE-DROP | 7 | 4 | 2 | 56 | Install Seal Kit SP-948-230-01 |\n| FM-SENSOR-ZERO-DRIFT | 6 | 3 | 2 | 36 | Zero calibration via PROC-PUMP-CALIBRATION |\n| FM-VALVE-SEAT-LEAK | 6 | 2 | 3 | 36 | Flush lines with bleach; replace V-04 |\n| FM-OPTICS-LAMP-DEGRADATION | 5 | 3 | 1 | 15 | Replace lamp L-01 every 2000 hours |\n\nAll field interventions performed under Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 must be validated with digital NIST manometer records logged directly into the Field Service Platform before clearing machine status to OPERATIONAL.",
        "thumbnailUrl": null,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.832Z"
      }
    ],
    "chunks": [
      {
        "id": "8cc5b998-35e4-4b40-a357-341e76bd4ba5",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "The BioMed Analyzer X200 is a fully automated, random-access clinical chemistry analyzer capable of executing up to 800 photometric tests per hour. Analytical precision relies on synchronous closed-loop coordination between the Fluidics Aspiration/Dispense manifold, the 12-wavelength diffraction grating photometer, and dual robotic pipetting arms with capacitive liquid level detection.\n\nThis technical manual provides authorized Field Service Engineers (FSE) with factory diagnostic thresholds, calibration procedures, alarm code resolution trees, and safety compliance directives.",
        "pageNumber": 1,
        "sectionTitle": "1. System Description & Analytical Architecture",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 512,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 100,
          "normTop": 22.7,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 12.6
        },
        "chunkType": "TEXT",
        "tokenCount": 95,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.961Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "957c17bc-8df3-4c41-b247-fbe0850af582",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "BIOHAZARD & HIGH VOLTAGE MANDATORY WARNING: All patient sera and fluidic waste lines must be treated as potentially infectious. Wear PPE (gloves, eye protection). Mains AC line voltages (100-240V) exist within the rear power distribution bay. Adhere strictly to LOTO protocols.",
        "pageNumber": 1,
        "sectionTitle": "Safety Directives",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 422,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 65,
          "normTop": 38.5,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 8.2
        },
        "chunkType": "WARNING",
        "tokenCount": 52,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.974Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "08e5c160-e1e3-47c2-9928-485bc61789cc",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "Hydraulic Operating Parameter Limits:\n\n| Operating Parameter | Nominal Target | Min Allowable | Max Allowable | Unit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Manifold Baseline Pressure | 120.0 | 114.0 | 126.0 | kPa |\n| Degasser Vacuum Level | -80.0 | -85.0 | -75.0 | kPa |\n| Dispense Syringe Stroke | 250.0 | 249.5 | 250.5 | uL |\n| De-bubble Purge Velocity | 50.0 | 45.0 | 55.0 | uL/s |\n| Sensor Zero Offset Limit | 0.0 | -1.2 | +1.2 | kPa |",
        "pageNumber": 2,
        "sectionTitle": "2.1 Hydraulic Operating Parameter Limits",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 532,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 140,
          "normTop": 15.2,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 17.7
        },
        "chunkType": "TABLE",
        "tokenCount": 88,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.980Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "ccf870a7-2c70-4d67-a190-dd82a4a15120",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "• Syringe Dispense Pump P-102 (P/N 948-230-01): 250 uL ceramic piston displacement mechanism.\n• Manifold Pressure Transducer PS-23 (P/N 948-510-23): Piezo-resistive stainless sensor on central block.\n• Solenoid Pinch Valve V-04 (P/N 948-310-04): 3-way high-velocity PTFE isolate valve.\n• Replacement Plunger Seal Upgrade Kit (P/N SP-948-230-01): Mandated by Service Bulletin SB-2026-014.",
        "pageNumber": 2,
        "sectionTitle": "2.2 Critical Fluidic Components & Part Numbers",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 412,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 85,
          "normTop": 37.2,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 10.7
        },
        "chunkType": "SPECIFICATION",
        "tokenCount": 74,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.984Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "27e5b061-2e67-47bf-9f62-0bdfe5242e7a",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "STEP 1: Line Depressurization & Safety Verification\nOpen Service Utilities > Fluidics Diagnostics > Depressurize Manifold. Verify digital readout drops to 0.0 kPa.\n\nSTEP 2: Physical Pressure Transducer Calibration Check\nConnect NIST-traceable Digital Manometer 948-CAL-01 to Quick-Disconnect test port TP-FL-01 on the central manifold.\nExecute 3-minute continuous DI water prime sequence at 50 uL/s.",
        "pageNumber": 3,
        "sectionTitle": "3. Diagnostic Tree: Alarm Code E1045 - Setup",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 552,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 110,
          "normTop": 16.4,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 13.9
        },
        "chunkType": "PROCEDURE_STEP",
        "tokenCount": 78,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.988Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "bbe3b8f6-b2ed-442b-89a6-5fd9c02adb92",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "DECISION BRANCH A: Physical Manometer vs Telemetry Divergence\n• If physical manometer reads within 114.0 - 126.0 kPa, but software telemetry reports < 114.0 kPa:\n  Cause: Transducer drift or zero-offset error in Pressure Sensor PS-23 (P/N 948-510-23).\n  Corrective Action: Recalibrate zero offset via PROC-PUMP-CALIBRATION. If offset exceeds +/- 1.2 kPa, replace sensor with assembly SP-948-510-23.",
        "pageNumber": 3,
        "sectionTitle": "3. Diagnostic Tree: Alarm Code E1045 - Branch A (Sensor Drift)",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 427,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 95,
          "normTop": 34.1,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 12
        },
        "chunkType": "PROCEDURE_STEP",
        "tokenCount": 82,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.994Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "03725540-0a68-4eec-8333-b946ba78573b",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "DECISION BRANCH B: True Physical Pressure Decay\n• If physical manometer ALSO reads < 114.0 kPa or exhibits decay > 1.5 kPa over 60 seconds:\n  Cause: Mechanical seal bypass in Syringe Pump P-102 or internal micro-tearing in Solenoid Valve V-04.\n  Corrective Action: Replace P-102 ceramic plunger wash seals using Upgraded Kit SP-948-230-01. Refer to Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 for proper torque specifications (1.2 Nm).",
        "pageNumber": 3,
        "sectionTitle": "3. Diagnostic Tree: Alarm Code E1045 - Branch B (Mechanical Bypass)",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 307,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 95,
          "normTop": 49.2,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 12
        },
        "chunkType": "PROCEDURE_STEP",
        "tokenCount": 86,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:15.999Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "b9b403c5-e200-4b83-9510-b052ee4cf6e7",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "FMEA Matrix & Service Bulletin Compliance:\n\n| Failure Mode Code | Severity | Occur | Detect | RPN | Mandatory Action Protocol |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FM-FLUIDICS-PRESSURE-DROP | 7 | 4 | 2 | 56 | Install Seal Kit SP-948-230-01 |\n| FM-SENSOR-ZERO-DRIFT | 6 | 3 | 2 | 36 | Zero calibration via PROC-PUMP-CALIBRATION |\n| FM-VALVE-SEAT-LEAK | 6 | 2 | 3 | 36 | Flush lines with bleach; replace V-04 |\n| FM-OPTICS-LAMP-DEGRADATION | 5 | 3 | 1 | 15 | Replace lamp L-01 every 2000 hours |",
        "pageNumber": 4,
        "sectionTitle": "4. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 Compliance & FMEA",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 522,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 130,
          "normTop": 17.7,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 16.4
        },
        "chunkType": "TABLE",
        "tokenCount": 92,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-23T03:44:16.002Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "cb0c3100-a173-4339-a323-8ae35e2e6ab1",
        "documentId": "4d26fd7d-d00a-4c6c-b396-301eb16d9f3c",
        "chunkText": "All field interventions performed under Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 must be validated with digital NIST manometer records logged directly into the Field Service Platform before clearing machine status to OPERATIONAL.",
        "pageNumber": 4,
        "sectionTitle": "Quality Assurance & Field Authorization Sign-Off",
        "boundingBox": {
          "x": 40,
          "y": 427,
          "width": 532,
          "height": 60,
          "normTop": 38.5,
          "normLeft": 6.5,
          "normWidth": 86.9,
          "normHeight": 7.6
        },
